# Scene Generation Policy

NEVER generate or modify .tscn files directly.

Godot scene files (.tscn) have a complex serialization format that breaks easily
when edited outside the Godot Editor. Even small errors cause scenes to fail loading.

## When asked to create a scene, instead:
1. Provide the GDScript file(s) for that scene
2. Write step-by-step instructions for manually setting up the scene in Godot Editor:
   - Which root node type to use
   - Which child nodes to add and their names
   - Which script to attach
   - Which properties to set in the Inspector
   - Which signals to connect

## Example output format:
Создание сцены Sphere.tscn (вручную в Godot Editor):
Создай новую сцену, корневой узел: RigidBody2D, переименуй в "Sphere"
Добавь дочерний узел: CollisionShape2D (форма: CircleShape2D, radius: 8)
Добавь дочерний узел: Sprite2D (texture: res://assets/sprites/sphere_1.png)
Прикрепи скрипт: res://scenes/pachinko/Sphere.gd
В Inspector → RigidBody2D: gravity_scale = 1.5, linear_damp = 0.1